<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Dun Nechtain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/685">685</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Nechtansmere</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Dun Nechtain, or Nechtansmere, was fought on 20 May 685 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bridei-son-of-beli">Bridei son of Beli</a> and the Northumbrians under King Ecgfrith, who was killed. The Pictish victory destroyed the Northumbrian army and ended English domination over the Picts and much of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-dun-nechtain.jpg" alt="Battle of Dun Nechtain" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Greenshed · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pictish_Stone_at_Aberlemno_Church_Yard_-_Battle_Scene_Detail.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 684 his army raided Brega in Ireland, and in 685 he led an invasion of Pictland that ended in disaster at the <b>Battle of Nechtansmere</b>, where the Pictish king Bridei son of Beli killed him and destroyed his army.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-northumbria">Kingdom of Northumbria · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Their greatest victory came on 20 May 685, when Bridei son of Beli defeated and killed the Northumbrian king Ecgfrith at <b>Dun Nechtain</b>, often called Nechtansmere, ending Northumbrian domination north of the Forth.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-picts">Kingdom of the Picts · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Bridei son of Beli destroyed the Northumbrian army at <b>Dun Nechtain</b> in 685, ending English dominance in the north. Óengus son of Fergus, from 729 to 761, defeated rivals and even campaigned against Dál Riata and Strathclyde.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-fortriu">Kingdom of Fortriu</a></li></ul></section>
